   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Dear Group,<div>I have setup app with Rstudio on mac OS without problem. Now I want to install Shiny server on a centos 5.11 server.</div><div>I did:</div><div>$sudo yum install R</div><div>$sudo su - -c &quot;R -e \\&quot;install.packages(&#39;shiny&#39;, repos=&#39;<a href=\"https://cran.rstudio.com/&#39;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cran.rstudio.com/&#39;&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792394559147000&amp;usg=AOvVaw053RLDG9eh-IlOlEImvcTp\">https://cran.rstudio.com/&#39;</a>)\\&quot;&quot;</div><div>I got an error message:</div><div>package ‘shiny’ is not available (for R version 3.2.3) <br></div><div><br></div><div>I also tries with R.3.1.1, same issue.</div><div><br></div><div>Any idea ?</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks.</div><div><br></div><div>Ping</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "9gUF13SUCAAJ",
