     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Thu, Feb 25, 2016 at 3:28 PM, Joe Cheng <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">j...@rstudio.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">I think you need to go back to your original command then, but replace the https with http (in the CRAN mirror URL). It&#39;s not ideal, sorry. <br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\">On Thu, Feb 25, 2016 at 1:19 PM Ping Hu &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">p...@lbl.gov</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi, Joe,<div>just tried:</div></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">sudo su - -c &quot;R -e \\&quot;</span>options(download.file.method = &#39;libcurl&#39;);<span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">install.packages(&#39;shiny&#39;, repos=&#39;</span><a href=\"https://cran.rstudio.com/&#39;\" style=\"font-size:12.8px\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cran.rstudio.com/&#39;&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792394559156000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0gPfmeLkmHT8ftO6CIZTZP\">https://cran.rstudio.com/&#39;</a><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">)\\&quot;&quot;</span><br></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><br></span></div></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">I got this:</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><br></span></div><div></div></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">&gt; options(download.file.method = &#39;libcurl&#39;);install.packages(&#39;shiny&#39;, repos=&#39;<a href=\"https://cran.rstudio.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cran.rstudio.com/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792394559156000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0xu-A1F-RRSog_HGm8zYly\">https://cran.rstudio.com/</a>&#39;)</span></div></div></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">Installing package into ‘/usr/lib64/R/library’</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">(as ‘lib’ is unspecified)</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">Warning: unable to access index for repository <a href=\"https://cran.rstudio.com/src/contrib\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cran.rstudio.com/src/contrib&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792394559156000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3Engzd9RhIDGok3dtLptC3\">https://cran.rstudio.com/src/contrib</a>:</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">  download.file(method = &quot;libcurl&quot;) is not supported on this platform</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">Warning message:</span></div></div></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">package ‘shiny’ is not available (for R version 3.2.3) </span></div></div></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">This is the same message I got before.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">on server, I used su -  then enter the root password. When I run the command you suggested, I ran as root. This is how this server was set up.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">Ping</span></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Thu, Feb 25, 2016 at 12:56 PM, Joe Cheng <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">j...@rstudio.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Can you try this instead?<div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\">sudo su - -c &quot;R -e \\&quot;<span style=\"font-size:small\">options(download.file.method = &#39;libcurl&#39;);</span><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">install.packages(&#39;shiny&#39;, repos=&#39;</span><a href=\"https://cran.rstudio.com/&#39;\" style=\"font-size:12.8px\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cran.rstudio.com/&#39;&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792394559156000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0gPfmeLkmHT8ftO6CIZTZP\">https://cran.rstudio.com/&#39;</a><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">)\\&quot;&quot;</span></div></div><div><br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Thu, Feb 25, 2016 at 9:21 AM,  <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">p...@lbl.gov</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Dear Group,<div>I have setup app with Rstudio on mac OS without problem. Now I want to install Shiny server on a centos 5.11 server.</div><div>I did:</div><div>$sudo yum install R</div><div>$sudo su - -c &quot;R -e \\&quot;install.packages(&#39;shiny&#39;, repos=&#39;<a href=\"https://cran.rstudio.com/&#39;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cran.rstudio.com/&#39;&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792394559156000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0gPfmeLkmHT8ftO6CIZTZP\">https://cran.rstudio.com/&#39;</a>)\\&quot;&quot;</div><div>I got an error message:</div><div>package ‘shiny’ is not available (for R version 3.2.3) <br></div><div><br></div><div>I also tries with R.3.1.1, same issue.</div><div><br></div><div>Any idea ?</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks.</div><div><br></div><div>Ping</div></div><span><font color=\"#888888\"><span><font color=\"#888888\"><span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;Shiny - Web Framework for R&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">shiny-discus...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion on the web visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/shiny-discuss/365fcfff-9e2a-415b-80ed-eb9dbf25c004%40googlegroups.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/shiny-discuss/365fcfff-9e2a-415b-80ed-eb9dbf25c004%2540googlegroups.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792394559156000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1lrpBjzeofstp0JOxuYhqg\">https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/shiny-discuss/365fcfff-9e2a-415b-80ed-eb9dbf25c004%40googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792394559156000&amp;usg=AOvVaw09VlnoOsKfyHlwDdPgnBgd\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.<br>\r\n</font></span></font></span></font></span></blockquote></div><span><font color=\"#888888\"><br></font></span></div><span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n</font></span></blockquote></div><span><font color=\"#888888\"><br><br clear=\"all\"><div><br></div></font></span></div><span><font color=\"#888888\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\">-- <br><div><div>Ping Hu, Ph.D</div>\r\n<div>Lawrence Berkeley National Lab</div>\r\n<div><a href=\"tel:510-486-5908\" value=\"+15104865908\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">510-486-5908</a></div>\r\n<div><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">p...@lbl.gov</a></div></div>\r\n</div></font></span></blockquote></div>\r\n</blockquote></div><br><br clear=\"all\"><div><br></div>-- <br><div class=\"gmail_signature\"><div>Ping Hu, Ph.D</div>\r\n<div>Lawrence Berkeley National Lab</div>\r\n<div><a href=\"tel:(